(6583668, 981582, 108580, '<td valign="top">Smoothest asphalt I''ve ever seen. Portrait Pro? hehe.<br/>Really nice shot of the bridge. unique. Post is also very crisp and contrasty. Love the duotone effect. Well done.</td>', 'Smoothest asphalt I''ve ever seen. Portrait Pro? hehe.Really nice shot of the bridge. unique. Post is also very crisp and contrasty. Love the duotone effect. Well done.', '2011-11-03 11:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6583685, 981560, 47906, '<td valign="top">You really have a great perspective/vantage point in this photo. I love the expanse of the overall landscape and the view this vista provides. <br/> <br/>I also love the lighting of the shot, The shadows and the illimunated areas that the clouds have created are lovely and provide a lot of interest in the forground and peaks of interest in the background to give a great feeling of depth in the photo. <br/> <br/>Your composition and sharpness are good, I really like the use of the rule of thids for the placement of the river, and the placement of the top of the mountain range as well. <br/> <br/>My only issue is the area in which the sun is setting it is very blown out and screams for attention first over the entire beautiful scene you have placed before is. Perhaps an hdr shot might have helped in this regard?<br/> <br/>Not voting, only commenting. Hope that you find this comment helpful.</td>', 'You really have a great perspective/vantage point in this photo. I love the expanse of the overall landscape and the view this vista provides.  I also love the lighting of the shot, The shadows and the illimunated areas that the clouds have created are lovely and provide a lot of interest in the forground and peaks of interest in the background to give a great feeling of depth in the photo.  Your composition and sharpness are good, I really like the use of the rule of thids for the placement of the river, and the placement of the top of the mountain range as well.  My only issue is the area in which the sun is setting it is very blown out and screams for attention first over the entire beautiful scene you have placed before is. Perhaps an hdr shot might have helped in this regard? Not voting, only commenting. Hope that you find this comment helpful.', '2011-11-03 12:20:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6583690, 980823, 108580, '<td valign="top">Sublime long exp. Love the colours and the stars peeping through. No guesses who''s work this is...erm or similar too! :)</td>', 'Sublime long exp. Love the colours and the stars peeping through. No guesses who''s work this is...erm or similar too! :)', '2011-11-03 12:25:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6583691, 981088, 108580, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work.</td>', 'Beautiful work.', '2011-11-03 12:26:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6583694, 981642, 47906, '<td valign="top">The technicals on this photo are really nice. The DOF is spot on deep enough to keep the sharp detail in the wing but fast enough to stop him in flight without blur. <br/> <br/>Your sharpness is great, I like that the wings are very detailed, and that you can make out the eye nicely. The composition is really nice as well. I like that the bird falls upon the intersecting points of the upper horizontal and the left vertical, makes it more powerful. <br/> <br/>I also love that you left the hills in the background and did not try to get a blue sky behind as it gives you a sense of where he may be flying to perhaps. <br/> <br/>The only thing that I might suggest, or try to do differently would to be closer to the heron, perhaps being able to see the eye more could give a stronger feel to the shot perhaps.<br/> <br/>Not Voting, only commenting.</td>', 'The technicals on this photo are really nice. The DOF is spot on deep enough to keep the sharp detail in the wing but fast enough to stop him in flight without blur.  Your sharpness is great, I like that the wings are very detailed, and that you can make out the eye nicely. The composition is really nice as well. I like that the bird falls upon the intersecting points of the upper horizontal and the left vertical, makes it more powerful.  I also love that you left the hills in the background and did not try to get a blue sky behind as it gives you a sense of where he may be flying to perhaps.  The only thing that I might suggest, or try to do differently would to be closer to the heron, perhaps being able to see the eye more could give a stronger feel to the shot perhaps. Not Voting, only commenting.', '2011-11-03 12:31:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6583701, 979254, 16046, '<td valign="top">Best in show, congratulating in advance!</td>', 'Best in show, congratulating in advance!', '2011-11-03 12:42:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6583702, 980098, 47906, '<td valign="top">I really love the serene feeling that this photo gives. <br/> <br/>Your diagonal in the foreground along with the ones created by the mountains give a great depth. The positioning of your horizon along the lower horizontial aides this also.Very good technicals. The slight reflections that are in the calm water are also really nice addition that gives a bit of eye candy/interest to the photo overall. <br/> <br/>The details/texture of the mountains are really great, I makes me think I can reach out and touch them. I like how you broke down the back mountain ranage as well to start and end on your verticals. <br/> <br/>The only things I could think of that might possibly make the photo better is to either have a more contrasty blue sky to give more seperation of the sky and the mountains, or perhaps for you to step back a couple feet and perhaps reposition yourself to include the reflection of the main mountains in the lake as well.<br/> <br/>Not Voting, Only commenting. Hope you found this comment helpful.</td>', 'I really love the serene feeling that this photo gives.  Your diagonal in the foreground along with the ones created by the mountains give a great depth. The positioning of your horizon along the lower horizontial aides this also.Very good technicals. The slight reflections that are in the calm water are also really nice addition that gives a bit of eye candy/interest to the photo overall.  The details/texture of the mountains are really great, I makes me think I can reach out and touch them. I like how you broke down the back mountain ranage as well to start and end on your verticals.  The only things I could think of that might possibly make the photo better is to either have a more contrasty blue sky to give more seperation of the sky and the mountains, or perhaps for you to step back a couple feet and perhaps reposition yourself to include the reflection of the main mountains in the lake as well. Not Voting, Only commenting. Hope you found this comment helpful.', '2011-11-03 12:43:27.000000', NULL, 1),
